We all know that Martin Short is funny. What we don&#8217;t know is how he endured a Job-like series of personal tragedies, from the early deaths of his parents and brother to his more recent losses of his wife and daughter. That&#8217;s what we learn in Lawrence Kasdan&#8217;s &#8220;Marty, Life Is Short,&#8221; nominated for three Primetime Emmys (Documentary or Special, Directing, and Editing). And Short himself is not only up yet again for his comedy performance in Netflix&#8217;s &#8220; Only Murders in the Building &#8221; Season 5, as well as Best Comedy, but also Best Game Show Host for ABC&#8217;s &#8220;Match Game.&#8221;

When Short&#8217;s old chum Kasdan suggested making a documentary about him, the comedian demurred. &#8220;I&#8217;m Canadian,&#8221; he said in a Zoom interview. &#8220;We&#8217;re a little more reserved. I&#8217;d also written a book in 2014, in which I&#8217;d been open. Then, Larry left me an eight-minute message on my phone. [He said that] I should do it because it&#8217;s important for life. [He imitates Kasdan&#8217;s signature nasal voice.] I heard it, and I said, &#8216;OK, I guess I have to do it because he kept saying &#8220;he and Ron,&#8221; and I love Ron Howard.'&#8221; Related Stories &#8216;The Pitt,&#8217; &#8216;All Her Fault,&#8217; and More Among Nominees for The DARCYS 2026 TIFF Will Honor Penélope Cruz, Lee Chang-dong, Fan Bingbing, Helen Mirren, Isabelle Huppert, and More

Short launched his relationship with Kasdan while starring in Kasdan&#8217;s production of the ill-fated &#8220;Cross My Heart&#8221; (1987). &#8220;We became great friends on the film,&#8221; he said. &#8220;Sometimes, you make the decision of saying, &#8216;I&#8217;m not going to let that person go.&#8217; We both made that, and that was 40 years ago.'&#8221;

Luckily for documentarian Kasdan, Short had been running a camera on his life for decades. Another buddy, Steven Spielberg, also supplied some intimate footage. The cinematic gold in this film is the peek into the remarkable Hollywood community Short and his beloved late wife Nancy Dolman built around them. We see Tom and Rita and Steve and Kate and many more familiar faces splashing, playing, making jokes, enjoying their camaraderie.

&#8220;I&#8217;ve been asked through the years, &#8216;What&#8217;s it like to be friends with Tom Hanks, Steven Spielberg? What are they like?'&#8221; said Short. &#8220;They&#8217;re just playful and friends. They just happen to be famous.&#8221;

